@startsalt
' Screen: Fork Script Modal
' User Stories:
'   - As a tester, I can fork a specific version of a script into a new script
'   - As a tester, the new slug is auto-derived from the new name but I can override it
'   - As a tester, I am shown an error if the new slug already exists

{
  == Fork Script ==
  ..
  {+
    <b>Forking from:</b>
    checkout-flow-test  <b>·</b>  <i>v2  (published 2026-05-08)</i>
    <i>Checksum: sha256:4f3a9c…</i>
  }
  ..
  {
    <b>New Script Name</b> <color:red>*</color>
    "checkout-flow-test-copy                   "
  }
  ..
  {
    <b>New Slug</b> <i>(auto-derived, editable)</i>
    "checkout-flow-test-copy                   "
  }
  ..
  {+ <color:red><b>⚠ Slug conflict</b></color>
  <i>A script with slug "checkout-flow-test-copy" already exists.</i>
  <i>Please choose a unique slug for the fork.</i> }
  ..
  <i>The fork will be created as a draft. No runs will be copied.</i>
  ==
  {
    [ Cancel ]  |  [ Fork Script ]
  }
}

@endsalt
